      "p0001-n0013-l0009"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In the second question, combining the social network analysis and the actual situation of football matches, we found three performance indicators: one team's total number of passes in one match, average contribution to the team and pass-possession rate, and four team level processes: aggregation, extension, tempo and connected configuration ratio. They were then combined with goal difference as the independent variable to draw the scatter plots and conduct multiple linear regression analysis. Finally, three significant variables that can effectively measure the level of team cooperation were selected and the performance model of passing network passed the test as a whole at a 95% significance level. And Root MSE equals to 1.5, which is of low level. The Huskies team is then described from three aspects: structure, configuration and dynamics."
  },
